[#:seon.task{:name "delivered-errors-carry-no-result-handle",
            :kind :function,
            :intent
            "A core error recorded during an agent's call (another thread included) reaches the reply's `:seon.repl/errors` as `seon.error/value` plus count and branch, but with no result handle or dig form: the agent can reach the whole recorded error only by knowing to pull [`:seon.error/signature` s] with the observation selector. Reproduce: in SCI as agent X, @(future (`seon.fault/fault!` env (ex-info \"async\" {:probe/async 1}) {`:seon.agent/id` X ...})) answers :errors [{`:seon.error/signature` … `:seon.error/message` \"async\"}] without :probe/async or any handle. Correct (errors spec, 'Every error in a reply's :errors and :diagnostics carries its result handle'): each delivered error carries a handle or requery form that answers the whole recorded value. Proof: an evaluation that records a core fault answers :errors whose handle reads the fault's ex-data.",
            :must-read
            #{seon.render.transcript/branch-errors
              seon.turn/fault-window}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-runtime-duration"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Give `seon.render.transcript/runtime-duration` a complete Malli contract that checks what its boundary is for, with the cheapest schema that checks it (`docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md`): registered names, every input and output, the error variants it returns. A contract that refuses a real value (a reaching test, a live call, your probe) is a finding, not friction: if the contract misread the value's shape, fix the contract and cite the observed shape; if the producer emits a bad value, keep the contract, file a task on the producer naming `seon.render.transcript/runtime-duration` in its must-read with the exact form, the refused value's essence and the Malli explain, and say so in your reply. Never widen to :any, [:maybe ...] or :map to go green. Done when `seon.contracts/gaps` answers [] for it and its reaching tests stay green and no slower."
             :must-read #{seon.render.transcript/runtime-duration seon.contracts/gaps}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/architecture/contracts-guide.md"}}]
